  <section class="wrap fiche-body">
    <div>
      <h2>The vibe</h2>
      <p>A campsite tucked between fine sand and sun-drenched hills in Hyères, where dogs are explicitly welcome — even in the establishment's restaurant, a detail rare enough to be worth mentioning.</p>

      <h2>What to know before you book</h2>
      <p>A few minutes away, Le Mérou beach (the only officially dog-friendly beach in Hyères) is accessible, as is the Giens peninsula for beautiful walks on a lead. Porquerolles island, reachable by a shuttle that accepts dogs for free, is also within reach from Hyères.</p>
      <div class="callout">Coco's tip: the ferry shuttles to Porquerolles from Hyères accept dogs on a lead at no extra charge — a lovely excursion to plan during your stay.</div>

      <h2>Nearby</h2>
      <p>Camping Les Palmiers, also in Hyères and dog-friendly, is another option 300m from the beach if this one is full.</p>
    </div>

